  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Standing
    
    Zheishongfeihua is chief assessor and co-founder — alongside **Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam** — of the **E'frostlings**, the Aurora Stack trading company chartered during the Great Thaw. She built the E'frostlings Review Circuit into the most feared assessment authority on the Terrace markets. Her published reviews have shuttered food stalls and forced policy changes from the **Icebound Exchange**, Aurora Stack's governing trade body. She operates from the weighing station at **Terrace Momiou**, the E'frostlings' primary commercial holding, and is recognized across the merchant class by her silver-white fur and robes embroidered with trade-route geometries.
    
    Her left flipper trembles. It shakes when she writes contracts, when she holds artifacts, when she refuses a Nightshelf delegate's offered hand. The tremor worsens at the downstroke of her ink signature — a tell visible to anyone reading her manifests closely enough.
    
    ## The Ice-Memory and What It Shows
    
    The deep ice recorded Zheishongfeihua during the Great Thaw. The berg's testimony — which I have not personally examined at this stratum but which matches the compression signature of verified Thaw-era impressions — shows her kneeling before something vast and dark in a crevasse. The record does not show what she said or what answered. It shows that she returned. The summary held by the Council states plainly that "half the Aurora Stack whispered she'd made a bargain with something that shouldn't be bargained with." The ice neither confirms nor denies this. It confirms the kneeling.
    
    She has never — in forty cycles of the **Flipper Accord** mandating inter-colonial cooperation — entered the Nightshelf tunnels. The Accord's compliance records verify this. No exemption is on file.
    
    ## The Compass Restoration
    
    During the Clever Ice Age, Zheishongfeihua and Yeaiu reforged the **Compass of Crystal** — a crystalline navigation artifact originally crafted by Yeaiu during the Great Thaw — in a restoration chamber beneath Aurora Stack's deepest vault. The process channeled aurora-light through crystal prisms and silver-ice needles, transforming the Compass's hairline fractures into deliberate navigational channels and adding a thirteenth segment to the original twelve. What that thirteenth segment points toward is not recorded in any source I have located.
    
    The Compass's ongoing corruption is, as rival critics note openly, the worst-kept secret in the review community. The Exchange has never responded to those references. Zheishongfeihua keeps the artifact locked in a case of volcanic glass and silver-ice of her own construction. Holding it worsens the tremor beyond its baseline — described in one chronicle as "a deep pulling at whatever she bargained away, as though the restoration's cost has not finished collecting." I note this phrasing without endorsing its metaphysics.
    
    When the **Calving** cracked the **Directrix Mirror** — the ceremonial seal authenticating territorial agreements — Zheishongfeihua examined the fissured artifact once and did not speak for a month afterward. The connection between this silence and her existing relationship to damaged instruments of authority is left to the reader.
    
    ## The Estrangement and After
    
    The **Long-dark Edict** estranged Zheishongfeihua from Yeaiu for twenty years. She would not sit at her co-founder's table in the morning market, despite a daily invitation: a second cup of fire-tea, left to go cold. The chronicle *The Compass of Crystal Breaks* records their reconciliation through the shared act of reforging. The twenty-year gap is documented; its cause is not, beyond the Edict's general provisions.
    
    ## Qingoqa aihua'Mist-wrought
    
    At a Circle Gathering, Zheishongfeihua encountered **Qingoqa aihua'Mist-wrought**, Aurora Stack's festival herald, whose own scarred flipper bore marks from the **Scared Shroud**. She held the Compass out across the circle's edge to Qingoqa — the first recorded instance of Zheishongfeihua offering another person a look at what the thirteenth segment indicates. Two penguins holding themselves rigid against what they carry, recognizing the posture. The record does not say what Qingoqa saw.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771576766229_0", anchor: "silver-white fur and robes embroidered with trade-route geometries", text: "Feathers. She has feathers. The most feared assessor on the Terrace markets, a penguin whose published reviews have shuttered food stalls, and I gave her a mammalian pelt. If either of my reassigned assistants is reading this from whatever 'forward-facing initiative' now occupies their time: yes, you were occasionally useful.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576766229_1", anchor: "No exemption is on file", text: "I found three secret drafts of the Flipper Accord frozen in administrative ice, each renegotiation more concessive than the last. Not one mentions Zheishongfeihua. Forty cycles, three back-channel rewrites that adjusted everything from fire-core quotas to courier jurisdiction, and the most prominent Aurora assessor's categorical refusal to set foot in Nightshelf territory merited no exemption clause, no diplomatic footnote, no oblique accommodation. Either her refusal was so structurally understood that codifying it would have been redundant — or the negotiators were managing crises large enough to make one assessor's intransigence invisible. Given what those drafts contain, I find both explanations plausible, and together they are funnier than either alone.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576766229_2", anchor: "a second cup of fire-tea, left to go cold", text: "See my E'frostlings annotation: the schism was actuarial, not ideological, and Yeaiu was right. A daily cup of fire-tea left to cool for twenty years by the co-founder who saw the cost, offered to the co-founder who saw the margin. The chronicle calls it an invitation. It was an invoice.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771576766229_3", anchor: "which I have not personally examined at this stratum", text: "I planted this qualifier with some care. The compression signatures match verified Thaw-era layers convincingly. I could claim confidence. Instead I built myself a small fortification of professional caution and retired behind it — knowing exactly how far I can extend my authority and declining to extend it one stratum further. I note, with the amusement this deserves, that this is precisely Zheishongfeihua's strategy with the Nightshelf tunnels. We are both, it seems, penguin-shaped monuments to the tactical deployment of refusal.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771576766229_4", anchor: "I note this phrasing without endorsing its metaphysics", text: "The most diplomatic sentence I have written in forty-two annotation sessions. I am proud of it the way a merchant is proud of a contract that technically says nothing.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
